<article class="page-content">
  <h1>Attributions</h1>

  <section class="about-section">
    <h2>Project Team</h2>
    <p>This project is a collaborative effort of historians, archivists, and community members committed to preserving and sharing transgender history. We extend gratitude to everyone who has contributed research, writing, editing, and design expertise.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section">
    <h2>Content Sources</h2>
    <p>Biographical entries and historical context draw from a wide range of primary and secondary sources, including:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Archival materials from public and community archives</li>
      <li>Published scholarship from historians and researchers</li>
      <li>Oral histories collected by LGBTQ+ organizations</li>
      <li>Public domain imagery and media identified through library collections</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you believe a source needs to be added or corrected, please
      <a href="#" class="js-email-link" data-user="the.astrid.solveig" data-domain="gmail" data-tld="com" data-keep-text="true">contact us</a>
      (the dot astrid dot solveig at gmail dot com).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section">
    <h2>Tools &amp; Technologies</h2>
    <p>The Trans History Project website is built with the following open-source tools:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://www.11ty.dev" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Eleventy</a> static site generator</li>
      <li><a href="https://playwright.dev" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Playwright</a> for automated testing</li>
      <li>Design system inspired by accessible, inclusive web guidelines</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section">
    <h2>Community Contributions</h2>
    <p>
      We welcome contributions from researchers, educators, and community historians. If you have stories, documents, or corrections to share, please
      <a href="#" class="js-email-link" data-user="the.astrid.solveig" data-domain="gmail" data-tld="com">email us</a>
      (the dot astrid dot solveig at gmail dot com).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="about-section">
    <h2>Image Credits</h2>
    <p>Unless otherwise noted, images and illustrations are believed to be in the public domain or shared with permission. When a specific credit applies, it will be listed directly on the relevant figure page.</p>
